---js
const numberOfLatestNewsToShow = 10;
---

{%- css %}{% include "public/css/message-box.css" %}{% endcss %}


<section class="profile" aria-label="About Marius">
	<div class="portrait-column">
		<img class="headshot" src="./headshot.png" alt="Marius Mosbach" fetchpriority="high" loading="eager">
	<div class="contact-links">
		<a href="mailto:marius.mosbach@uni-saarland.de" class="contact-link" aria-label="Email" title="Email"><i class="fa-solid fa-envelope" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">Email</span></a>
		<a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=O7RwHEkAAAAJ&hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="contact-link" aria-label="Google Scholar" title="Google Scholar"><i class="fa-solid fa-graduation-cap" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">Google Scholar</span></a>
		<a href="https://x.com/mariusmosbach" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="contact-link" aria-label="X" title="X"><i class="fa-brands fa-x-twitter" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">X</span></a>
	</div>
	</div>
	<div class="profile-intro">
	<p>
		I am an Associate Professor in the
		<a href="https://www.uni-saarland.de/en/department/lst.html">Department of Language Science and Technology</a>
		at <a href="https://saarland-informatics-campus.de/en/">Saarland University</a>
		and a Scientific Director at the <a href="https://www.dfki.de/en/web">German Research Center for Artificial Intelligence (DFKI)</a>.
		Previously, I was a postdoctoral researcher
		at <a href="https://mila.quebec/en">Mila – Quebec AI Institute</a> and <a href="https://www.mcgill.ca/">McGill University</a> in Montréal.
		I obtained my PhD in Computer Science from <a href="https://saarland-informatics-campus.de/en/">Saarland University</a>
		in Saarbrücken. I am a member of <a href="https://ellis.eu/">ELLIS.</a>
	</p>
	<p>
		My research is in the field of Natural Language Processing and Artificial Intelligence. I work on
		understanding the capabilities, limitations, and  inner workings of large language models (LLMs).
		I am particularly interested in model adaptation. This includes developing interpretability methods to study how models change as a result of adaptation, LLM unlearning,
		and continual learning.
	</p>
	</div>
</section>

<div class="home-details">


{% set newsCount = collections.news | length %} {% set latestNewsCount =
newsCount | min(numberOfLatestNewsToShow) %} {% if latestNewsCount != 0 %}

<div class="section-heading"><h2 class="latest-news">News</h2></div>
{% endif %}

<ul class="news-list">
	{% for item in collections.news | reverse | head(numberOfLatestNewsToShow) %} {% if
	not item.data.hidden %}
	<li>
		<time class="meta-label" datetime="{{ item.date | htmlDateString }}">{{ item.date | readableDate("LL/yyyy") }}</time>
		<span>{{ item.templateContent | safe }}</span>
	</li>
	{% endif %} {% endfor %}
</ul>

</div>
